<title>FINLAND: ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULT.</title>
<headline>ICE HOCKEY-WORLD CHAMPIONSHIP RELEGATION ROUND RESULT.</headline>
<dateline>TAMPERE, Finland 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Ice hockey world</p>
<p>championship relegation round result on Friday:</p>
<p>Germany 4 Norway 2 (0-0 0-1 4-1)</p>
<p>Scorers:</p>
<p>Germany - Bradley Bergen (40:50), Peter Draisaitl (47:32),</p>
<p>Mirko Ludemann (52:20), Jochen Hecht (58:23).</p>
<p>Norway - Michael Smithurst (33:51), Atle Olsen (46:54).</p>
<p>Penalties: Germany 12 minutes and Leo Stefan 10 minutes</p>
<p>(misconduct), Norway 10 minutes.</p>
<p>Attendance: 5,590.</p>
<p>Standings:</p>
<p>			   P   W  D  L   F   A   Pts</p>
<p> 1. Latvia	     4   3  0  1  24  10    6</p>
<p> 2. Slovakia	   4   3  0  1  11   8    6</p>
<p> 3. Italy		4   2  1  1  15  12    5</p>
<p> 4. France	     4   2  0  2  11  15    4</p>
<p> 5. Germany	    5   2  0  3   8  17    4</p>
<p> 6. Norway	     5   0  1  4  11  18    1</p>
<p>Remaining matches: Slovakia v Latvia, France v Italy</p>
<p>(Saturday).</p>
<p>Norway finish last in pool A and must play in a regional</p>
<p>qualifying group for a place in the 1998 A pool world</p>
<p>championship tournament in Switzerland.</p>
</text>
